      "content": "i get that you have to be careful with the medical stuff but it feels way too specific to just be a \"condition.\" the heat signatures are so detailed, like i can see the different temperatures in his paws vs his back. and the electrical hum... it's not just noise, it has a rhythm to it. it feels more like i'm finally seeing the underlying layer of reality that everyone else is just blind to. if this is a transition period, how do people usually handle the sensory overload? is there like a way to stabilize these new connections so i don't crash?",
